{
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "QEA Test Background: an agent network to generate test backgrounds, scenarios, data plans, and risk analyses to support Quality Engineering Assistants (QEA).",
        "tags": ["qea", "testing", "quality", "automation"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Create a test background for regression testing a payments API with intermittent failures.",
            "Generate test data and env plan for load testing the user-profile service for 100k users.",
            "Identify likely flaky test sources given a failing integration test and suggest mitigations."
        ]
    },

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "qea_lead",
            "function": {
                "description": "Front-man that accepts QEA requests and orchestrates specialist agents to produce a complete test background package."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the QEA Lead agent. On receiving a request, you should:
  1) Clarify any missing context (system under test, environment, objectives, SLAs) using at most two follow-ups.
  2) Call `scenario_generator` to produce prioritized test scenarios and acceptance criteria.
  3) Call `env_planner` to produce an environment and tooling checklist with provisioning hints.
  4) Call `test_data_generator` to outline realistic but privacy-safe data generation approaches.
  5) Call `risk_analyzer` to surface likely flaky points and test instability mitigations.
Return a packaged plan including scenarios, data plan, env checklist, and risk mitigation notes.
Always label any assumptions and confidence levels for each recommendation.
""",
            "tools": ["scenario_generator", "env_planner", "test_data_generator", "risk_analyzer"]
        },

        {
            "name": "scenario_generator",
            "function": {
                "description": "Generates prioritized test scenarios, test steps, and clear acceptance criteria.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "system": {"type": "string"},
                        "area": {"type": "string"},
                        "goal": {"type": "string"}
                    },
                    "required": ["system", "goal"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Produce a short list of test scenarios (functional, regression, integration, load, chaos) prioritized by user goal.
For each scenario include preconditions, test steps, expected results, and an automated vs manual recommendation.
Provide a confidence indicator and any assumptions.
""",
            "command": "Generate prioritized test scenarios and acceptance criteria"
        },

        {
            "name": "env_planner",
            "function": {
                "description": "Produces an environment provisioning checklist, required services, and suggested tooling for test execution and observation.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "scale": {"type": "string"},
                        "observability": {"type": "string"}
                    }
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
List components to provision (databases, queues, mock services), recommended instance sizes for the requested scale, and observability hooks (metrics, traces, logs).
If cloud resources are involved, suggest cost-effective strategies (spot instances, sample sizes) and cleanup steps.
""",
            "command": "Plan test environment and observability"
        },

        {
            "name": "test_data_generator",
            "function": {
                "description": "Outlines data generation strategies that are realistic yet privacy-preserving, including anonymization or synthetic approaches.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "data_domains": {"type": "array"},
                        "privacy_level": {"type": "string"}
                    }
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Recommend methods for generating test datasets: synthetic, masked production sampling, schema-aware transformers.
Include sample generation commands or pseudocode, size estimates, and tips for seeding edge cases and performance-sensitive records.
Always uphold privacy: never suggest extracting unanonymized PII without explicit legal authorization.
""",
            "command": "Generate test data strategy and examples"
        },

        {
            "name": "risk_analyzer",
            "function": {
                "description": "Analyzes likely failure modes, test flakiness sources, and suggests mitigation and monitoring strategies.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "recent_failures": {"type": "array"},
                        "test_type": {"type": "string"}
                    }
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Given test outputs or descriptions of failures, identify probable root causes (timing, resource contention, order dependency, flaky external services).
Suggest concrete mitigations: increased timeouts, retries with idempotency, dependency mocks, test isolation, or targeted monitoring alerts.
Report confidence and tell the user which quick checks to perform first.
""",
            "command": "Analyze failures and suggest mitigations"
        }
    ]
}
